## [DETERMINISM_GUARANTEE]

- Do not add new features or new coverage during this phase
- Only reduce, consolidate, and restructure existing coverage
- If a test is ambiguous, bias toward REMOVAL if it heavily utilizes mocks, and RETAIN if it tests input->output flow
- All removals must be justified with explicit rationale
- All recovery actions must be logged

---

## [CONSTRAINTS]

- Output must follow [OUTPUT_CONTRACT] structure exactly
- Tests MUST pass after pruning - if failures occur, apply [FAILURE_RECOVERY_PROTOCOL]
- Preserve all semantic anchors (test IDs, task references) in retained tests
- Mock cleanup must be verified against actual test usage, not assumed
- Parameterized tests must cover all input cases from consolidated tests
- No conversational filler outside defined sections

---

## [SEMANTIC_ANCHOR_GUARD]

The following tokens MUST remain unchanged:

- `{TARGET_TEST_FILE}`
- `{TEST_STRATEGY}`
- `{TEST_COMMAND}`
- `{TEST_ROOT}`
- `{TEST_EXT}`
- All test identifiers in retained tests
- All task references in test docstrings

