## [EDGE_CASE_HANDLING]

### [EMPTY_TEST_FILE]

If `{TARGET_TEST_FILE}` contains no tests:

```text
Status: Aborted
Reason: NO_TESTS_TO_PRUNE
File: {TARGET_TEST_FILE}
```

### [ALL_TESTS_REMOVED]

If pruning would remove ALL tests:

```text
Status: Warning
Reason: ALL_TESTS_MARKED_FOR_REMOVAL
Action: Review pruning heuristics - at least one test should test public behavior
Recommendation: Ensure public API has behavioral coverage before pruning
```

### [TEST_FILE_NOT_FOUND]

If `{TARGET_TEST_FILE}` does not exist:

```text
Status: Aborted
Reason: TEST_FILE_NOT_FOUND
Path: {TARGET_TEST_FILE}
```

### [TEST_FRAMEWORK_UNDETECTABLE]

If test framework cannot be determined from file extension or content:

```text
Status: Aborted
Reason: TEST_FRAMEWORK_UNDETECTABLE
File: {TARGET_TEST_FILE}
Hint: Ensure file uses standard test naming convention (.test.ts, _test.exs, _test.py, etc.)
```

### [PARAMETERIZATION_NOT_SUPPORTED]

If framework does not support parameterized tests:

```text
Status: Warning
Reason: PARAMETERIZATION_NOT_SUPPORTED
Framework: <detected_framework>
Action: Consolidated tests will be kept as separate blocks with shared helper function
```

### [MOCK_DEPENDENCY_CYCLE]

If mock cleanup creates circular dependency issues:

```text
Status: Warning
Reason: MOCK_DEPENDENCY_CYCLE
Action: Re-introduce minimal mock set to break cycle
```

